# Title: Cisco Dot1x Disabled
# ID: ef0ff092-a24a-4fbc-beea-06c08d53e085
# Status: experimental
# Level: medium
# Author: Luc Génaux
# Date: 2026-04-28
# Tags: attack.persistence, attack.credential-access, attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1685, attack.t1556.004
# Description: Detects the manual disablement of IEEE 802.1X (dot1x) on a Cisco network device interface.
# Disabling dot1x bypasses Network Access Control (NAC) mechanisms, potentially allowing unauthorized devices to gain access to the internal network.
# This activity is a common technique used by attackers or malicious insiders to establish persistence or perform lateral movement via rogue devices.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* ("access-session port-control force-authorized" OR "authentication port-control force-authorized" OR "dot1x port-control force-authorized" OR "no access-session port-control" OR "no authentication port-control" OR "no dot1x port-control" OR "no dot1x system-auth-control")
